  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The medium-sized leaves of this attractive New Jersey laceleaf have the coloring of the better-known red 'Baldsmith' and the finely cut lacy texture of the green 'Chantilly Lace'. New leaves are bright red, becoming salmon-pink before changing to pink-red over green for the summer. Fall colors are brilliant orange to scarlet. New red leaves are produced all summer and make an attractive contrast to the pink-green background of older leaves. The changing colors Acer are more striking in full sun. 'Watnong' forms a Gelderen. Acer palmatum"
  },
